  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Microsoft has $412M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Microsoft won 158 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.6M, and obligations are down 22.4% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $333M, making the Department of Defense the largest buyer of Microsoft in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services is Microsoft’s largest market with $235M in obligations, followed by Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services with $157M. Smaller markets include Other Computer Related Services at $16.3M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $2.7M. Historical obligations show a peak of $531M in FY25 and a decline to $412M in FY26. The data reflect partial current-year totals, so FY2026 figures are fiscal year to date rather than full-year totals. This snapshot highlights concentration in defense buying and in systems and infrastructure services, and it shows a measurable year-over-year contraction in obligations for Microsoft so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall year over year?",
        "body": "Microsoft obligated $412M in FY2026 to date, and obligations are down 22.4% year over year. The Department of Defense remains the largest buyer with $333M, but overall federal obligations to Microsoft are lower than the prior fiscal year total of $531M in FY25. The decline coincides with a shift toward concentrated spending in a few markets such as Computer Systems Design Services and Computing Infrastructure Providers, which together account for the bulk of FY2026 obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Microsoft’s largest federal buyers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Microsoft’s largest buyer in FY2026 to date with $333M in obligations. The Department of Agriculture is the second-largest buyer with $36.9M, followed by the Department of State with $15.8M and the Social Security Administration with $12.3M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top market at $235M, followed by Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $157M."
      }
    ]
  },
